  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197630",
      "title": "What Is Navigation?",
      "lectureOrder": 91,
      "videoOrder": 88,
      "sourceHash": "7057da43174e92a0aa31a83a09769aa0f8f576fc00151a51a0ccb943ce627840",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.06,
          "end": 5.83,
          "en": "So what exactly is navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.83,
          "end": 9.5,
          "en": "in the context of a React Native app?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.5,
          "end": 11.16,
          "en": "Well, in the end it just means that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.16,
          "end": 13.48,
          "en": "we can move between different screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.48,
          "end": 16.72,
          "en": "as we did it in this little game we built before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.72,
          "end": 18.71,
          "en": "but as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.71,
          "end": 21.37,
          "en": "there we had no real way of going back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.37,
          "end": 23.48,
          "en": "from one screen to the previous screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.48,
          "end": 24.94,
          "en": "we had no animations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.94,
          "end": 28.503,
          "en": "and we simply replaced one screen with another.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 30.53,
          "en": "And that could be fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.53,
          "end": 31.75,
          "en": "but in many apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.75,
          "end": 35.48,
          "en": "you want a more fine-grained navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.48,
          "end": 37.73,
          "en": "For example, in one of the demo apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.73,
          "end": 40.8,
          "en": "we're going to build in this course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.8,
          "end": 43.58,
          "en": "you will be able to go forward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.58,
          "end": 46.88,
          "en": "to a specific screen and then go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.88,
          "end": 49.1,
          "en": "if you wanna go to the previous screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.1,
          "end": 51.85,
          "en": "We're also going to explore how you could add taps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.85,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "to switch between different screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 58.25,
          "en": "and how you can combine different navigation patterns.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.25,
          "end": 60.69,
          "en": "And that's what I mean with navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.69,
          "end": 62.82,
          "en": "in Native mobile apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.82,
          "end": 65.33,
          "en": "and therefore also in React Native apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.33,
          "end": 66.74,
          "en": "since we use React Native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.74,
          "end": 69.363,
          "en": "to build Native mobile apps in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 70.28,
          "end": 72.87,
          "en": "Now, when we think about navigation in the web,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 72.87,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 77.38,
          "en": "then, of course, we just enter a URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 77.38,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "and we land on a page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 80.5,
          "en": "and we can then use links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.5,
          "end": 83.58,
          "en": "to navigate to different sub pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 83.58,
          "end": 85.86,
          "en": "On mobile apps it's a bit different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.86,
          "end": 88.67,
          "en": "There we don't have such a URL,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.67,
          "end": 91.18,
          "en": "instead we navigate by tapping buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91.18,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "and going from one screen to another to another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 97.13,
          "en": "and then maybe back and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 97.13,
          "end": 99.15,
          "en": "And in this section, we're going to learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 99.15,
          "end": 102.05,
          "en": "how we can implement such a navigation pattern,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 102.05,
          "end": 103.57,
          "en": "or to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 103.57,
          "end": 106.83,
          "en": "these different navigation patterns I talked about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 106.83,
          "end": 108.65299999999999,
          "en": "in React Native apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 109.53,
          "end": 110.61,
          "en": "Now, for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 110.61,
          "end": 114.37,
          "en": "I'm back in a brand new React Native app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 114.37,
          "end": 116.93,
          "en": "You find this starting project attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 116.93,
          "end": 118.87,
          "en": "And it's a very simple starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 118.87,
          "end": 121.16,
          "en": "which we used before in the course already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 121.16,
          "end": 125.27,
          "en": "with just a dummy hello world screen showing up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 125.27,
          "end": 126.803,
          "en": "on our emulators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 127.75,
          "end": 129.51,
          "en": "But we're going to build up on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 129.51,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "And as a first demo app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 134.41,
          "en": "we're going to build a meals app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 134.41,
          "end": 139.41,
          "en": "where users will be able to choose a category of meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 140.41,
          "end": 142.01,
          "en": "they're interested in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 142.01,
          "end": 145.55,
          "en": "and then they will be able to explore different meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 145.55,
          "end": 147.23,
          "en": "that belong to that category,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 147.23,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "and view the details about a specific meal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 154.4,
          "en": "Now, the categories and meals data will be provided to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 154.4,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "but that is what we'll build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 158.53,
          "en": "and as you can already see here in this finished app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 158.53,
          "end": 160.48,
          "en": "which we are going to build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.48,
          "end": 163.67000000000002,
          "en": "there we can navigate between those different screens,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.67000000000002,
          "end": 165.23,
          "en": "forward and backward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 165.23,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "So that's what we'll build here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 170.96,
          "en": "Now for that, we have of this starting project here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.96,
          "end": 172.76,
          "en": "this starting app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 172.76,
          "end": 174.25,
          "en": "And as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 174.25,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "we need some dummy data so that we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 182.75,
          "en": "show all these categories we want to be able to navigate to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 182.75,
          "end": 183.73,
          "en": "For data attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 183.73,
          "end": 186.76,
          "en": "you find a dummy data JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 186.76,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "And in your expo project that you set up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 192.91,
          "en": "you can create a data folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 192.91,
          "end": 194.33,
          "en": "and in that data folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 194.33,
          "end": 197.293,
          "en": "you can copy in that dummy data JS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 198.2,
          "end": 202.91,
          "en": "And this file gives you some dummy meals and category data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.91,
          "end": 204.86,
          "en": "that was set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 204.86,
          "end": 209.13,
          "en": "Now, in addition, you also find a models sub file attached,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
